post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
listello is installed. Nothing starts by itself. To use it:

  sudo systemctl enable --now listello-core.socket

then open "listello" from the application menu. The first time, it asks whether to start
listello every time you log in. Stopping it (in its window or from the tray icon) gives the
Touch Bar back to the keys the Mac draws itself.

Configuration: copy /usr/share/listello/config.toml to /etc/listello/config.toml and edit that
copy. /usr/share/listello/config.example-dock.toml is a fuller example with a Dock.
MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'MSG'
listello was upgraded. Reload the system units, then stop the renderer; it starts again by
itself the next time listello is started:

  sudo systemctl daemon-reload
  sudo udevadm control --reload
  sudo systemctl stop listello-core
  sudo systemctl enable --now listello-core.socket
MSG
}

pre_remove() {
  systemctl disable --now listello-core.socket >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
}
